					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656#post-4772546</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656/scp-139#post-4772546</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2020 16:01:11 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>A Random Day</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1841781</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>The slipstream fascist depiction of this Foundation does a fantastic job setting the article's tone and helping it carve a distinct niche for itself against similar stories like <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-2357">SCP-2357</a> and <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3393">SCP-3393</a>.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656#post-4772466</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656/scp-139#post-4772466</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2020 14:15:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Nagiros</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>4665703</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Eparch was used first in <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-4015">SCP-4015</a> and is defined within that article as…</p> <blockquote> <p>&quot;Eparch&quot; is an esoteric class denoting an object classed as an SCP for its anomalous circumstances or relationships rather than for having anomalous effects.</p> </blockquote> <p>I decided against footnote-defining it because, like… well, it seems a bit tacky.</p> <p>And yes, ze/hir are being used as nb; the &quot;their&quot; is used in reference to the general population in-context instead of just Lucian.</p> <p>Glad you liked it!</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656#post-4772171</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656/scp-139#post-4772171</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2020 04:33:29 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Hugh Manatee</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3557786</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Love the ending. No idea what the object/containment class &quot;eparch&quot; is supposed to mean though.</p> <p>Had to pause and look up the ze/hir pronouns to be sure I was pronouncing &quot;hir&quot; correctly in my head. I see these are being used as non-binary rather than gender-neutral pronouns, given the usage of singular &quot;their&quot; in one place for an unknown person's spirit.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656#post-4766341</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656/scp-139#post-4766341</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 03 Sep 2020 21:55:48 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Suspicious Mr Guy</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3481354</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>A good story, simple setup, well written overall. I figured out that the reader is supposed to be lucian before the direct announcement, and that just made the twist of &quot;aha, they predicted me&quot; all the better. It gives the foundation a real ominous persona, and I <em>love it.</em> And the visual theme too&#8230; it all gives off massive &quot;shadow organization&quot; vibes, which is suprisingly something I don't feel all too often from articles.</p> <p>I'm glad we have this now that the old 139 is gone.</p> <p>+1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
