					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656#post-4765259</guid>
				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13690656/scp-139#post-4765259</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2020 14:52:44 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Raptie</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>1968091</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>So. When I read a story like this, the nonbinary pronouns tend to make me have a visceral reaction that's&#8230; It distracts me, and makes me think, &quot;Is it me necessary to have the character be like this?&quot;</p> <p>But&#8230; That's the thing, isn't it. The fact that I'm trying to find justification in the the usage of these nonstandard pronouns is <em>exactly the problem.</em></p> <p>It means that stories like this are so, so important because they continue to push the normalization of nonstandard pronouns, and I know eventually I won't even notice them.</p> <p>(What's really ironic is that I have this reaction and <em>I myself am enby.</em>)</p> <p>So, thank you. Thank you for pushing forward in the name of progress and tying it to a damn good story. &lt;3</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
